// expect: 1
// mn-arm-ground-instance-face — an arm whose handler fixes its effect's
// instance is still called at the op's declared face.
//
// `add` declares its parameter the effect's type variable, so every performer
// passes it as a word: a performer does not know which handler will answer.
// `fsum` fixes the instance at Float, so its arm reads `x` as f64. The arm is
// reached through its op-face adapter, which unboxes the word and calls the
// arm — from `main`'s own perform directly, and from `feed`'s through the
// named arm the walk resolves. 0.5 + 1.25 + 2.5 = 4.25.
//
// RED on boot 30a35888: the module did not assemble after a clean check
// (`undefined local variable "$x.f64"` — the arm's header signed the op's word
// while its body read f64). Signing the header at the handler's instance
// instead only moved the mismatch to the call (`expected [i32, f64] but got
// [i32, i32]`), which is what named the adapter.
effect Acc {
  add(x: a)
  get() -> a
}

handler fsum with s = 0.5 {
  add(x) => resume() with s = s + x,
  get() => resume(s),
}

fn feed() = add(2.5)

fn main() -> Int = {
  add(1.25)
  feed()
  if get() == 4.25 { 1 } else { 0 }
} ~> fsum
